re separate. So even if W6 is in a meld, I might still have another W6 in hand.\n\nThus, my current **live hand**: W6, W7, W8, T9, B6, B7, B8, F2 \u2014 8 tiles. Need to discard one.\n\nI have two potential chow structures forming:\n- W6-W7-W8: almost a chow, missing W5 or W9 to complete middle or end.\nWait: W6-W7-W8 is already a sequence! That\u2019s a chow: [W6,W7,W8].\n\nSimilarly, B6-B7-B8 is also a chow: [B6,B7,B8].\n\nSo actually, I may have:\n- Meld 1: [W4,W5,W6] (already declared)\n- Meld 2: [B5,B6,B7] (already declared)\n- Possible Chow in hand: [W6,W7,W8] and [B6,B7,B8] \u2014 but overlapping tiles.\n\nConflict: W6 is in both [W4,W5,W6] and potentially [W6,W7,W8] \u2014 but only 4 copies exist.\n\nCheck usage:\n- My meld uses one W6\n- I hold one W6 \u2192 total two\n- Previous player discarded W6 \u2192 third used\n- One W6 remains unshown \u2192 possible\n\nBut cannot use same tile twice. So if I already melded [W4,W5,W6], that W6 is fixed. The W6 in hand is a different copy \u2014 so I can use it.\n\nSame for B6, B7: used in [B5,B6,B7], but if I have another copy, I can form [B6,B7,B8].\n\nSo possibilities:\n- Concealed chow: [W6,W7,W8] \u2014 if I hold a W6 (not the melded one)\n- Concealed chow: [B6,B7,B8] \u2014 similarly\n\nBut I only have 8 live tiles: W6, W7, W8, T9, B6, B7, B8, F2\n\nSo yes \u2014 I can claim:\n- [W6,W7,W8] as a concealed chow\n- [B6,B7,B8] as another concealed chow\n\nBut I can\u2019t have both unless I have two W6s, two B6s, etc.\n\nLet\u2019s check availability:\n- W6: 4 total. Used: my meld (1), previous player discarded (1) \u2192 2 used. Unshown: 2 \u2192 so 2 left \u2192 possible I have one.\n- W7: 4 total. My hand has W7, across player has [W7,W8,W9] (used one W7), I have one \u2192 2 used? Across player used one, I hold one, previous history: I played W7? No \u2014 my history: Play W3, W9, W2 \u2014 no W7 played. Across played W7 once. So W7: one in their meld, one in my hand \u2192 2 used. Unshown: 3 \u2192 ok.\n- W8: 