\n\nAnswer: Play W5\n\nBut let's confirm valid actions: [Play B6; Play B5; Play W8; Play B7; Play W5] \u2014 yes, W5 is allowed.\n\nReason: W5 is the safest discard among the options, as it is less likely to complete an opponent's chow or pair compared to B5/B6/B7 or W8.\n\nSituation: I have three exposed chows and must discard one tile from my hand. Opponents have shown limited interest in Character-5 or Dots sequences. W5 appears to be the safest discard.\nEvaluation: Discarding B5, B6, or B7 risks completing a chow for an opponent in Dots, especially B6 which connects multiple sequences. W8 could help complete W789. W5 is less critical.\nReason: W5 is the least dangerous tile to discard based on opponents' discards and melds.\nAnswer: Play W5"}
