ave had W6 and W8, and claimed W7.\n\nBut earlier I played W3, W9, W2 \u2014 but not W6 or W8.\n\nAfter Chi B6, my hand changed.\n\nBut now, current hand is said to include B5, B6, B7 \u2014 which is **impossible** because they were used in a meld formed via Chi.\n\nTherefore, the **hand listing is incorrect**.\n\nBest interpretation: The **current hand** should be what remains **after all actions**, excluding melded tiles.\n\nFrom history, after forming [W4,W5,W6] (via Chi W5), [B5,B6,B7] (via Chi B6), [W6,W7,W8] (via Chi W7), and discarding many tiles, my current hand must consist of tiles not used in melds.\n\nThe valid actions are: [Play B6; Play B5; Play W8; Play W2; Play B7]\n\nThese are **discard options** \u2014 so my hand must currently contain these tiles.\n\nBut if B5, B6, B7 are in a meld, I can\u2019t discard them unless I have duplicates.\n\nGiven the unshown counts and play history, the most plausible explanation is that **I have duplicate tiles**, and the melds use one set, while hand has another.\n\nBut B7 is particularly tight.\n\nAlternative: The meld [B5,B6,B7] is **not** using the same tiles as hand \u2014 meaning I have **two sets**.\n\nBut that would require two full chows of B5-B7 \u2014 6 tiles \u2014 but only 4 copies each \u2014 impossible.\n\nThus, **the only logical conclusion is that the hand listing includes tiles erroneously**.\n\nGiven the valid actions are discards, and they include B5, B6, B7, W8, W2, it means my hand currently contains **at least one of each**: B5, B6, B7, W8, W2.\n\nBut since I formed [B5,B6,B7] via Chi, I cannot have those tiles unless I drew new ones later.\n\nLooking at history: After \"Chi B6\", I played W3, J3, W9, T2, F2, T8, W2, T9, F2, T3, Chi W7, then played W7, T5, B8, W5 \u2014 no draw mentioned.\n\nBut in Mahjong, after each discard, you draw, unless claiming.\n\nWhen I performed \"Chi B6\", I did not draw \u2014 I claimed the discard, added to meld, then discarded a tile (W3).\n\nSame for Chi W7 \u20